.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt PKG 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pkg
.Nd install, remove and update packages
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm sync
.Nm
.Cm install Ar package | Ar archive No ...
.Nm
.Cm remove Ar package No ...
.Nm
.Cm update Ar package | Cm all No ...
.Nm
.Cm search Ar pattern
.Nm
.Cm list Op Ar filter
.Nm
.Cm info Ar package
.Nm
.Cm rdeps Ar package
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is Novi's package manager.
Packages are
.Pa .pkg.tar.gz
archives with a MANIFEST; the format is described in
.Xr pkg-format 5 .
.Pp
.Cm sync
refreshes the index and
.Cm update
upgrades installed packages.
They are different operations and have different names deliberately.
.Bl -tag -width "install pkg|archive"
.It Cm sync
Fetch the repository index and verify its signature.
.It Cm install
Install packages, by name from the index or from a local archive.
Dependencies are resolved and installed first.
.It Cm remove
Remove packages.
Warns if something still depends on them and proceeds; see
.Cm rdeps .
.It Cm update
Upgrade installed packages, or all of them.
.It Cm search
Search the index.
.It Cm list
List what is installed.
.It Cm info
Print a package's MANIFEST.
.It Cm rdeps
List installed packages that depend on this one.
.El
.Ss Trust
The index is signed with Ed25519 and
.Cm sync
verifies it with
.Xr novi-verify 1
before believing a line of it.
Every package's SHA-256 comes from that index, so one signature covers
the whole repository, and the hash is checked again before an archive
is unpacked
.Em including
one already in the cache.
The index carries a
.Va valid-until
inside the signature, because a signature says genuine, not current.
.Pp
An archive whose hash does not match is refused.
A cached copy that fails is deleted; one in a repository directory is
skipped but left alone, because that is somebody's media.
.Ss File ownership
.Cm install
refuses a path another package owns, and refuses a path nothing owns.
A package may take over an unowned path only by declaring
.Va replaces-files=
in its MANIFEST, in which case the original is saved and
.Cm remove
puts it back.
.Fl -overwrite
is the operator's override and is deliberately not something a MANIFEST
can ask for.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width PKG_MIRROR -compact
.It Ev PKG_MIRROR
Override the configured mirror for one invocation.
.It Ev PKG_REPO
Directory of available archives.
Default
.Pa /var/cache/pkg/repo .
.It Ev PKG_ROOT
Alternate install root.
Note that this relocates where files land but not the install
database, so it is for building images, not for installing into
another running system.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/lib/pkg/installed" -compact
.It Pa /etc/novi/pkg.conf
Configuration.
See
.Xr pkg.conf 5 .
.It Pa /etc/novi/keys/novi-repo.pub
The repository public key.
.It Pa /var/lib/pkg/installed
The install database: one directory per package.
.It Pa /var/cache/pkg/archives
Downloaded archives.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Install the desktop from the repository on the installation medium:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# pkg sync
# pkg install novi-desktop
.Ed
.Pp
Find what would break before removing something:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ pkg rdeps zlib
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
mkpkg(1),
.Xr novi-state 1 ,
.Xr novi-verify 1 ,
.Xr pkg-format 5 ,
.Xr pkg.conf 5 ,
.Xr novi-slot 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 0006 describes the trust model,
.Pa /usr/share/doc/novi/rfcs/0006-package-repository-and-signing.md .
